# Crustum Broadcasting

Prefer package docs and the `broadcasting-development` skill for orientation.

@scoped(['config/broadcasting.php', 'config/bootstrap.php'])
## Broadcasting config
- Keep driver credentials and `options.host` / `port` / `path` / `scheme` aligned with the WebSocket server (or SaaS Pusher).
- Prefer `BroadcastingTrait` in tests when asserting sends; Null driver disables real delivery.
- Load `config/broadcasting.php` from bootstrap after manifest install.
@endscoped

@scoped(['config/channels.php'])
## Channel authorization registry
- Register private/presence auth with `Broadcasting::channel(...)` (closure or channel class).
- Public channels need no callback; missing private/presence registrations fail at `/broadcasting/auth`.
- Wildcards (e.g. `{order}`) bind to callback / `join()` args. Presence: return `false` or a member data array.
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/Broadcasting/**', 'src/**/*Channel.php'])
## Channel classes
- Prefer `{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake channel Order') }}` — implement `ChannelInterface::join(...)`.
- Register the class in `config/channels.php`; keep auth logic in the class.
@endscoped

@scoped(['config/routes.php'])
## Broadcasting auth routes
- Default endpoints: `/broadcasting/auth` and `/broadcasting/user-auth` (plugin routes).
- If plugin routes are off, register them explicitly or Echo private/presence joins 404.
- Allow CSRF for SPA auth POSTs per Broadcasting docs (one-time Application / middleware setup).
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/Event/**', 'src/**/*Broadcast*.php'])
## Broadcast events
- Implement `BroadcastableInterface` (`broadcastChannel`, `broadcastEvent`, `broadcastData`, `broadcastSocket`).
- Fire with `broadcast($event)` or Broadcasting helpers; use `toOthers()` to exclude the current socket.
- Queued broadcasts need a running queue worker.
@endscoped

@scoped(['src/Model/Table/**'])
## Model broadcasting
- Use model `BroadcastingTrait` + `BroadcastingTraitInterface` and behavior `Crustum/Broadcasting.Broadcasting` together.
- Configure channels/payload via setters or behavior config; disable when tests must not emit.
@endscoped

@scoped(['tests/**/*Broadcast*', 'tests/TestCase/**/*Broadcast*'])
## Broadcasting tests
- Use `Crustum\Broadcasting\TestSuite\BroadcastingTrait` to capture sends.
- Assert with `assertBroadcastSent`, `assertBroadcastSentToChannel`, payload/queued helpers from the trait.
@endscoped

@scoped(['webroot/js/**', 'resources/**/*.js', 'assets/**/*.js'])
## Echo client
- Auth endpoint: `/broadcasting/auth`.
- Match Echo key / host / port / path / TLS to Broadcasting options and the WS server.
@endscoped
